new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b13e5ce
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+## Deploying on one box
+
+Fizzy can run on a single Linux server with Docker: SQLite, the web process and background jobs in one container, and HTTPS from kamal-proxy. The database and uploaded files live on a Docker volume, so they survive the next deploy.
+
+### Fill in three things
+
+1. **Hostname** in `config/deploy.yml` (`x-host`). It must resolve to the server, accept SSH, and have ports 80 and 443 open. Fizzy will be at `https://that-host`.
+2. **Mail server** in `config/deploy.yml` (`x-mail-server`). Sign-in is a magic link, so this has to be a real SMTP server. Port 587 with STARTTLS is the default.
+3. **Secrets**, exported in the shell you run Kamal from:
+
+```sh
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE=$(bin/rails secret)
+export SMTP_USERNAME=your-smtp-user
+export SMTP_PASSWORD=your-smtp-password
+```
+
+Leave the SMTP variables unset only if that server relays without a login. Keep `SECRET_KEY_BASE` the same on every deploy or existing sessions are signed out. `.kamal/secrets` reads these from the environment — do not commit raw credentials.
+
+### Deploy
+
+From the repository root, on a machine that can SSH to the server and has Docker (Kamal builds the image there and serves it from a local registry):
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+That is Kamal's `kamal setup`: it installs Docker if the server does not have it, builds the image, and boots Fizzy. Later deploys are `bin/kamal deploy`.
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal logs
+bin/kamal console
+```
+
+### Notes
+
+- Jobs run in the web container (`SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA`). Do not add a jobs host. SQLite is on this box, and a second container would be a second writer.
+- The volume `fizzy_storage` is mounted at `/rails/storage`. To back that up as a directory, switch the volume line in `config/deploy.yml` to a host path such as `/var/lib/fizzy:/rails/storage`.
+- The image is pushed through a local registry Kamal starts on the server. You do not need Docker Hub.
+- A typical VPS is amd64. If the server is ARM, set `builder.arch` to `arm64`.
+- If SSH should use an IP while the public name is a hostname, set `servers.web` to the IP and keep `x-host` as the public name.
+- The From address on mail defaults to `Fizzy <fizzy@your-host>`. Set `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` if the mail server requires a specific address.
